<h1>metaphone</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An algorithm to code English words phonetically by reducing them to 16 consonant sounds.  A better variant is <a href="doubleMetaphone.html"><em>double metaphone</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="phoneticCoding.html"><em>phonetic coding</em></a> <a href="algorithm.html"><em>algorithm</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="jaroWinkler.html"><em>Jaro-Winkler</em></a>, <a href="caverphone.html"><em>Caverphone</em></a>, <a href="nysiis.html"><em>NYSIIS</em></a>, <a href="soundex.html"><em>soundex</em></a>, <a href="Levenshtein.html"><em>Levenshtein distance</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Many <a href="http://aspell.net/metaphone/" target="_blank">metaphone and double metaphone (Basic, C, Perl, and C++)</a> implementations. Apache codec implementations of  <a href="https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-codec/" target="_blank">soundex, Metaphone, and Double Metaphone (Java)</a>. 
<h2>More information</h2>
<p>
<strong>Andrew Binstock and John Rex</strong>. <em>Metaphone: A Modern Soundex<em>. Practical Algorithms For Programmers.  Addison-Wesley, 1995 pages 160-169. </p> <p> <strong>Gary Parker</strong>. <em>A Better Phonetic Search</em>. C Gazette, Vol. 5, No. 4 (June/July), 1990. </p> <p> <strong>Lawrence Philips</strong>. <em>Hanging on the Metaphone</em>. Computer Language, Vol. 7, No. 12 (December), 1990.
</p>

